.TH tummdb n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tummdb
.PP
Pure\-Tcl reader for the MaxMind DB (\fB.mmdb\fR) binary format.
.PP
\fBtummdb\fR resolves IPv4 and IPv6 addresses to their data records in GeoLite2, GeoIP2 and DB\-IP databases. It reads version 2.0 of the binary format and builds on \fBtclutils::tubin\fR for all binary primitives.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tubin 0.2
package require tclutils::tummdb 0.1
.CE
.SS "Open and close"
.CS
set h [::tclutils::tummdb::open /path/to/GeoLite2-City.mmdb]
# ... lookups ...
::tclutils::tummdb::close $h
.CE
.PP
\fBopen\fR loads the file into memory and returns a handle. It throws \fBTCLUTILS TUMMDB FORMAT\fR if the file is not a valid MaxMind DB.
.SS Metadata
.CS
set m [::tclutils::tummdb::metadata $h]
dict get $m database_type    ;# e.g. GeoLite2-City
dict get $m ip_version       ;# 4 or 6
dict get $m record_size      ;# 24, 28, or 32
.CE
.SS Lookup
.CS
set r [::tclutils::tummdb::lookup $h 81.2.69.142]
puts [dict get $r country iso_code]   ;# GB
puts [dict get $r city names en]      ;# London
puts [dict get $r location latitude]  ;# 51.5142
.CE
.PP
\fBlookup\fR returns the decoded record as a nested structure (maps become dictionaries, arrays become lists, localized names live under a \fBnames\fR sub\-dictionary), or the empty string if the address is not in the database.
.SS "Error codes"
.TS
l l.
Error code	Meaning
\fBTCLUTILS TUMMDB FORMAT\fR	File is not a valid MaxMind DB
\fBTCLUTILS TUMMDB HANDLE\fR	Unknown handle passed to a command
\fBTCLUTILS TUMMDB RECORDSIZE\fR	Unsupported tree record size
\fBTCLUTILS TUMMDB TYPE\fR	Unsupported data type in the record
.TE
.SS Notes
.PP
The whole database is held in memory while open. The interpretation of record fields (which keys exist) is defined by the database, not by this reader. \fBopen\fR and \fBclose\fR are intentionally not exported (they would clash with the Tcl built\-ins on \fBnamespace import\fR); call them fully qualified.
